{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1094696-2e-multiple-instances-of-phantom-glory","id":1094696,"title":"2E, multiple instances of Phantom Glory?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-19T15:18:41-07:00","id":1094696,"title":"2E, multiple instances of Phantom Glory?","content":"The wording on the Fairest Affinity for this contract is a bit wonky. The interpretation I get is that it allows the Fairest to send a friend (or enemy) into Twilight, but not at the same time that they themselves enter Twilight. Each person sent into the ephemeral must be sent via different instances of activating the contract. <br /> <br /> One or two of the STs at my LARP have gotten it into their head that a single Changeling can't have more than one iteration of the same Contract going at the same time. Because of this, I can send someone else into Twilight, but then I have to end the contract early (bringing that person back into the physical) if I want to then use the contract on myself. <br /> <br /> Phantom Glory is kind of a central power for my character in stealth or combat scenes and this latter interpretation doesn't feel right. There are a lot of mechanical issues that arise when sending any ally into Twilight and not being able to communicate or see them for the duration. The biggest of these issues is: how do I know when I should let them back out? <br /> <br /> I can't remember reading in any Changeling source book that a given contract can't be activated again on separate targets while the first effect is still in play. Is this actually a rule somewhere, or should I discuss the issue with my ST?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T18:22:06-07:00","id":1094738,"title":"","content":"I agree with you, but Changeling 2e hasn't been finalized yet so I don't know wjat the final form will look like yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T03:49:26-07:00","id":1094828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cardran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1094696-2e-multiple-instances-of-phantom-glory#post1094696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember reading in any Changeling source book that a given contract can't be activated again on separate targets while the first effect is still in play. Is this actually a rule somewhere, or should I discuss the issue with my ST?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see any such limitations in the RAW but I might be missing something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T05:09:32-07:00","id":1094838,"title":"","content":"I don't recall any thing saying you can only have one instance of a Contract active at once. You can't have multiple instances of a Contract on yourself, since you can't benefit from the same thing more than once. But, that's different from, say, using Murkblur on multiple different opponents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}